---
// PDF-97 D7, rewritten. The production-posture section: the page's answer
// to "can I depend on this". Its section id is `status`, the last id the
// published anchor set (`sections.ts`/`Navbar.astro`) reserves.
// (Deliberately not spelled as a literal `id=` example in this comment:
// `tests/test_website_contract.py`'s AR2/AR4 scan `website/src` for
// exactly that attribute shape, and a worked example here would double-
// count as one of its own targets -- the same reason `sections.ts` and
// `LicenseSummary.astro` give for the identical omission.)
//
// WHAT CHANGED AND WHY. The first version of this section answered a
// MAINTAINER's question. Two of its three cards pointed a reader at
// `BACKLOG.md` and `qa/FINDINGS-LEDGER.md` -- artifacts the same cards
// then admitted are not in the distribution -- and the third announced
// "Phase 1 (v1) complete", a term that means nothing outside the project.
// A signpost to a locked door is worse than silence: it spends the
// reader's attention advertising that they cannot look. Meanwhile the
// repository has an issue tracker nobody was told about and attested
// provenance on PyPI that nothing on the site mentioned.
//
// Three claims now, each ACTIONABLE and each verifiable in one click,
// with a verbatim source anchor into `README.md` checked by
// `tests/test_website_contract.py`'s `SOURCE_ANCHORS` table (D8): the
// output/exit-code contract is public API frozen at v1.0.0 (P1);
// publication is CI-only over OIDC with attested provenance (P2); a bug
// goes to the issue tracker and every fix lands in the changelog (P3).
//
// Four things this section still deliberately never names (D7, AC9): a
// sweep id, a commit sha, an open-finding tally, and a version number
// outside the one sanctioned, frozen phrase "public API from v1.0.0" --
// a historical fact that never rots, not a claim about the current
// release. `README.md`'s own `## Known issues` section remains the place
// where the maintainer's planning tree is disclosed to anyone reading
// this source tree beside it; this page does not restate it, because a
// website visitor cannot open it.
//
// Boundary with `ClosingCta.astro` (D7): the DCO line, the install
// command and the three ranked destinations are that component's, and
// this one does not restate them.
import { pick } from '../lib/i18n';

const issuesUrl = 'https://github.com/ArmandoHerra/pdf-tooling/issues';
const changelogUrl = 'https://github.com/ArmandoHerra/pdf-tooling/blob/main/changelog.md';
const releasesUrl = 'https://github.com/ArmandoHerra/pdf-tooling/releases';

const t = pick(Astro.url, {
  eyebrow: 'Production posture',
  heading: 'What you can depend on',
  lede: 'Three promises, and how to check each one.',
  contractTitle: 'Frozen contract',
  contractA:
    'The structured output shapes and the exit-code table are public API from v1.0.0. Breaking either takes a new major version and a ',
  contractB:
    ' change, so a script you write today keeps working across every minor and patch release.',
  deliveryTitle: 'How it reaches you',
  releasesLink: 'Releases',
  deliveryA:
    " are built and published by CI from a tag, over OIDC. That means the workflow holds no upload token at all, so nothing can be published from a developer's machine. Both files PyPI serves carry signed provenance, so you can check that what you installed was built from this repository.",
  troubleTitle: "When something's wrong",
  issueLink: 'Open an issue',
  troubleA:
    '. The command, the flags, the input and what you expected is enough to act on. Every fix that ships is in the ',
  changelogLink: 'changelog',
  troubleB: ', written by the commit that made it.',
}, {
  eyebrow: 'Postura de producci\u00f3n',
  heading: 'Con qu\u00e9 puedes contar',
  lede: 'Tres promesas, y c\u00f3mo comprobar cada una.',
  contractTitle: 'Contrato congelado',
  contractA:
    'Las formas de salida estructurada y la tabla de c\u00f3digos de salida son API p\u00fablica desde la v1.0.0. Romper cualquiera de las dos exige un cambio de versi\u00f3n mayor y un incremento de ',
  contractB:
    ', as\u00ed que un script que escribas hoy sigue funcionando en todas las versiones menores y de parche.',
  deliveryTitle: 'C\u00f3mo te llega',
  releasesLink: 'Las versiones',
  deliveryA:
    ' las construye y publica CI a partir de una etiqueta, sobre OIDC: el flujo de trabajo no guarda ning\u00fan token de subida, as\u00ed que nada se puede publicar desde la m\u00e1quina de alguien. El wheel y el sdist llevan procedencia atestiguada en PyPI, as\u00ed que puedes verificar que el artefacto que instalaste se construy\u00f3 desde este repositorio.',
  troubleTitle: 'Cuando algo sale mal',
  issueLink: 'Abre un issue',
  troubleA:
    ': con el comando, las banderas, la entrada y lo que esperabas es suficiente para actuar. Toda correcci\u00f3n que se publica queda en el ',
  changelogLink: 'changelog',
  troubleB: ', escrita por el commit que la hizo.',
});
---

<section id="status" class="u-crop mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-24">
  <p class="micro text-surface-400">{t.eyebrow}</p>
  <div class="u-reveal-rule mt-3 h-px w-full bg-line" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <h2 class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-surface-50 sm:text-4xl">
    {t.heading}
  </h2>
  <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg text-surface-300">
    {t.lede}
  </p>

  <dl class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
    <div class="card p-4">
      <dt class="micro text-primary-400">{t.contractTitle}</dt>
      <dd class="mt-2 text-sm leading-snug text-surface-200">
        {t.contractA}<code class="code-inline text-xs">schema_version</code>{t.contractB}
      </dd>
    </div>
    <div class="card p-4">
      <dt class="micro text-primary-400">{t.deliveryTitle}</dt>
      <dd class="mt-2 text-sm leading-snug text-surface-200">
        <a href={releasesUrl} class="text-primary-400 underline hover:text-primary-300"
          >{t.releasesLink}</a
        >{t.deliveryA}
      </dd>
    </div>
    <div class="card p-4">
      <dt class="micro text-primary-400">{t.troubleTitle}</dt>
      <dd class="mt-2 text-sm leading-snug text-surface-200">
        <a href={issuesUrl} class="text-primary-400 underline hover:text-primary-300"
          >{t.issueLink}</a
        >{t.troubleA}<a
          href={changelogUrl}
          class="text-primary-400 underline hover:text-primary-300">{t.changelogLink}</a
        >{t.troubleB}
      </dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
</section>
